 "issue": 1954,
 "issue_title": "Bug: select_dtypes should preserve row count for empty matches",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`ArFrame.select_dtypes()` raises `ValueError` when no columns match the dtype filter.\n\nThis differs from pandas-style selection behavior and from Arnio\u2019s current zero-column frame support. A dtype selection that matches no columns should be able to return an empty-column `ArFrame` while preserving the original row count.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`select_dtypes()` is useful in generic pipelines where the available column types may vary by dataset. Raising on an empty match forces users to add defensive pre-checks before every dtype selection, even though an empty result is a valid and useful outcome.\n\nArnio already supports zero-column frames in other paths, so this behavior is unnecessarily restrictive.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `arnio/frame.py`: `select_dtypes()` builds a `matched` list and raises `ValueError` when it is empty.\n- `arnio/frame.py`: `select_columns()` also rejects empty selections, so `select_dtypes()` cannot currently delegate to it for a zero-column result.\n- Existing zero-column frame tests show Arnio can preserve row counts for empty-column frames.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport arnio as ar\n\nframe = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame({\"age\": [1, 2], \"score\": [3.5, 4.0]}))\n\nresult = frame.select_dtypes(include=\"string\")\n\nassert result.shape == (2, 0)  # currently raises ValueError\n```\n\nAnother trigger:\n\n```python\nframe.select_dtypes(exclude=[\"int64\", \"float64\"])\n# currently raises ValueError instead of returning a zero-column frame\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nWhen the dtype filter is valid but matches no columns, return an `ArFrame` with:\n\n- the original row count\n- zero columns\n- no data loss in the original frame\n\n## Actual behavior\n\n`select_dtypes()` raises `ValueError: No columns match the dtype selection`.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nAdd a zero-column construction path for `select_dtypes()` when the filter itself is valid but `matched` is empty. Add focused tests for:\n\n- `include` with an absent dtype\n- `exclude` removing all columns\n- row count preservation\n- interaction with attrs metadata, if supported by the final implementation\n\n## References\n\n- `arnio/frame.py`\n- `tests/test_frame.py`\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1954",
 "pr": 1978,
 "pr_title": "fix: return zero-column ArFrame when select_dtypes matches no columns",
 "pr_body": "Fixes #1954\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n- `select_dtypes()` no longer raises `ValueError` when a valid dtype filter matches no columns\r\n- Returns a zero-column `ArFrame` preserving the original row count instead\r\n\r\n## Tests added\r\n- `include` with an absent dtype\r\n- `exclude` removing all columns\r\n- row count preservation\r\n- `attrs` metadata copied but not shared",
